  "fanTake": "Well, that was cathartic. Twenty to three at home against Pittsburgh is the kind of defensive clinic that reminds you why we've built our identity around that side of the ball, and frankly, we needed to see it after some of the chop-and-change the offense has been going through. Rhamondre Stevenson's three percent win probability added doesn't sound like much until you realize he was the most impactful player on the field—sometimes dominance in games like this is about doing the right thing at the right time rather than putting up gaudy numbers. We didn't turn the ball over, our defense held the Steelers to three points, and we got a win at Gillette that felt clean and uncomplicated. Still, there's plenty of work to do before we're satisfied with this team.",
